From: iEDA loongarch64 port <tsuibin@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] log: link glog/gflags dynamically when building static iEDA

The upstream static build hardcodes libglog.a and libgflags.a, which makes
CMake emit "-Wl,-Bstatic -lglog -lgflags". AOSC OS only ships shared glog
0.7.1 / gflags 2.2.2 (no -static packages), so the final link fails with
"cannot find -lglog". Use the plain dynamic library names instead; the
resulting iEDA binary still works normally.

diff --git a/src/utility/log/CMakeLists.txt b/src/utility/log/CMakeLists.txt
index a35d6b8..d0d99f7 100644
--- a/src/utility/log/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/utility/log/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -41,8 +41,10 @@ endif()
 add_definitions(-DGLOG_USE_GLOG_EXPORT)
 
 if(BUILD_STATIC_LIB)
-  SET(LINK_glog   "libglog.a")
-  SET(LINK_gflags "libgflags.a")
+  # loongarch64 AOSC ships glog/gflags as shared libs only (no lib*.a).
+  # Link them dynamically so the final iEDA binary can link successfully.
+  SET(LINK_glog   "glog")
+  SET(LINK_gflags "gflags")
   ADD_LIBRARY(log STATIC ${SRC})
 else()
   SET(LINK_glog   "glog")
